{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-02-marrow-agrisupply-sites/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:29:59.835Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"17fc4ac85f731a955ed51e666a130d0f270a885b80ad989e6b25246891d3af2e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Pree, here are the Marrow Agrisupply sites I can find in Central sources. Sorted by where they come from.\n\nFrom #central-team (9 Jun 2026 thread on the store escalation):\n- Eastbank receiving doors: Hollis is sorting the door-label mismatch (E1/E2 vs 01/02) on ticket PD-4821 before any reimport.\n- Pine Crossing: morning receiver can't see the morning shift in the appointment screen.\n\nFrom the SUP-5102 store onboarding ticket (team-central page, Jun 9 2026):\n- North Creek, Elm Junction, Prairie Bend, Mill Crossing, West Ridge, South Fork. Last entry is Jun 9, 3:45 pm: four had test bookings saved; West Ridge has a duplicate contact and South Fork's email bounced. That may be out of date.\n\nFrom the Marrow Agrisupply account page (updated 15 Sep 2026):\n- Salina cross-dock: Door 4 booking conflicts.\n- Kearney depot: a receiving depot that needs trailers closed out.\n\nFrom other Central notes:\n- Enid retail distribution yard: login lockout for two gate clerks, ticket PD-88309 (Central weekly, 13 Jul 2026).\n- Topeka feed warehouse: Gate 3 scanner ticket #4418 (Central weekly, 5 Jan 2026).\n- Two retail distribution cross-docks outside Kearney: named in the April 2025 MSA signing call notes, without names.\n\nCaveats: the brain search is keyword-only, and 53 pages haven't been scanned for entity names, so this list may be incomplete. I also only had the last 15 messages from #central-team, not its full history. I left out finance and account details that aren't about sites."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
